  (text "NOTES\nU5: OR-ing path A: battery / adapter\nU6: OR-ing path B: Pi 5 V (USB-C only bench mode)\nQ5: sees up to 13 V Vds when battery path wins\nC24: hot-loop cap: closest to VIN/GND\nU7: FCCM fixed 1.2 MHz (RT=GND); EN abs max 6 V -> open-drain pull-down only\nC26: soft start ~3.2 ms\nR21: Vout = 0.8 V x (1 + 31.6/10) = 3.33 V\nC29: optional feed-forward\nR22: INA226 #2 shunt, upstream of every socket bulk cap\nU8: I2C 0x41 (A0=VS, A1=GND): HaLow card current\nC31: pi-filter input cap\nFB1: verify rating at BOM step: >=4 A, <=30 mOhm\nJP1: cut to isolate the HaLow card rail\nQ8: pulls TPS62933F EN low when LTC2955 is off\nR23: high value: BENCH (Q9 on) must not load LTC_ENB, or Q7 cannot turn 5 V off (review P2)\nQ9: BENCH override: keeps 3.3 V on\nC32: EN has only a 0.7 uA pull-up: noise immunity\nJP2: close: HaLow 3.3 V forced on while the Pi 3.3 V is present" (at 15 113.26 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 79dcdc7e-7340-50f0-9f54-c13eee9e7556))
)
